The initialization proof is index-specific: every i in [0,95] has exactly one writer, thread i. For i < valid, that writer loads the valid input element; otherwise it stores zero without reading input. All 96 writers execute the same barrier before thread zero reads any shared value, and no thread subsequently modifies shared memory. Thread zero sums in increasing index order using round-to-nearest float additions. Same-stream ordering places the input copy before the kernel and the output copy after it; the completion event is recorded after both, and the host waits before reading or freeing buffers. These checks can report execution errors, but successful completion alone is not a proof of correctness—the participation and memory-ordering argument supplies that proof.

B’s wait references the first record of E—the record current when the wait was submitted. Interpreting “weight” as “wait,” recording E again does not retarget that already submitted wait; the later query reports the second record’s status. P2 can race with C1 because neither stream orders P2 after C1.

A permitted execution trace is:
1. A completes P1, storing 1, and completes the first record of E.
2. B’s wait is satisfied, but C1 has not yet performed its read.
3. A starts P2. While P2 is still unfinished, querying E after its second record returns not ready.
4. P2 stores 2 before C1 reads the allocation; C1 consequently reads 2 rather than P1’s 1.
5. P2 finishes and A completes the second record of E.
All stream-order constraints hold, yet the wrong generation is consumed. Overlapping reads and writes are also permitted; successful CUDA calls do not establish safe ownership.

The following complete program uses two slots. On reuse, A waits for that slot’s previous consumed event before overwriting it; B waits for its current ready event before reading it. First use skips the consumed wait because there is no previous consumer.

```cpp
// ownership.cu
#include <cuda_runtime.h>
#include <cstdio>
#include <cstdlib>

static void check(cudaError_t status, const char* call)
{
    if (status != cudaSuccess) {
        std::fprintf(stderr, "%s: %s\n", call,
                     cudaGetErrorString(status));
        std::exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
    }
}
#define CHECK(call) check((call), #call)

__global__ void producer(int* slot, int value)
{
    *slot = value;
}

__global__ void consumer(const int* slot, int* result)
{
    *result = *slot;
}

int main()
{
    constexpr int iterations = 8;
    cudaStream_t A, B;
    CHECK(cudaStreamCreateWithFlags(&A, cudaStreamNonBlocking));
    CHECK(cudaStreamCreateWithFlags(&B, cudaStreamNonBlocking));

    struct Slot {
        int* data = nullptr;
        cudaEvent_t ready{};
        cudaEvent_t consumed{};
        bool used = false;
    };
    Slot slots[2];
    for (auto& slot : slots) {
        CHECK(cudaMalloc(reinterpret_cast<void**>(&slot.data), sizeof(int)));
        CHECK(cudaEventCreateWithFlags(&slot.ready, cudaEventDisableTiming));
        CHECK(cudaEventCreateWithFlags(&slot.consumed,
                                       cudaEventDisableTiming));
    }

    int* results = nullptr;
    CHECK(cudaMalloc(reinterpret_cast<void**>(&results),
                     iterations * sizeof(int)));

    for (int i = 0; i < iterations; ++i) {
        Slot& slot = slots[i % 2];

        // Capture the previous consumed record before its next rerecord.
        if (slot.used) {
            CHECK(cudaStreamWaitEvent(A, slot.consumed, 0));
        }

        producer<<<1, 1, 0, A>>>(slot.data, i + 1);
        CHECK(cudaGetLastError());
        CHECK(cudaEventRecord(slot.ready, A));

        // Capture this generation's ready record before its next rerecord.
        CHECK(cudaStreamWaitEvent(B, slot.ready, 0));
        consumer<<<1, 1, 0, B>>>(slot.data, results + i);
        CHECK(cudaGetLastError());
        CHECK(cudaEventRecord(slot.consumed, B));
        slot.used = true;
    }

    // Final drain only; no host synchronization between iterations.
    CHECK(cudaStreamSynchronize(B));
    CHECK(cudaStreamSynchronize(A));

    int host_results[iterations];
    CHECK(cudaMemcpy(host_results, results, sizeof(host_results),
                     cudaMemcpyDeviceToHost));
    bool correct = true;
    for (int i = 0; i < iterations; ++i) {
        if (host_results[i] != i + 1) {
            std::fprintf(stderr, "iteration %d: got %d, expected %d\n",
                         i, host_results[i], i + 1);
            correct = false;
        }
    }

    for (auto& slot : slots) {
        CHECK(cudaEventDestroy(slot.ready));
        CHECK(cudaEventDestroy(slot.consumed));
        CHECK(cudaFree(slot.data));
    }
    CHECK(cudaFree(results));
    CHECK(cudaStreamDestroy(A));
    CHECK(cudaStreamDestroy(B));
    if (correct) std::puts("All results correct");
    return correct ? EXIT_SUCCESS : EXIT_FAILURE;
}
```

