Exact-once coverage proof: initially, lane l represents only input l. Before the offset-16 stage, treat that as the set of indices l + 32j below 19. Inductively, before an offset-d stage, lane l represents precisely the inputs at indices l + 2dj below 19. Its partner l + d represents l + d + 2dj below 19. These two sets are disjoint, and their union is precisely l + dj below 19. If l + d is outside the participating range, the partner set is empty, and skipping the addition preserves that same invariant. Thus after offset 1, lane 0 represents every input 0–18 exactly once. Broadcasting lane 0’s result returns that same computed sum to every caller.

Participation proof: every source is either a partner below 19 or the calling lane itself, so every source is named in `mask` and executes the collective. All nineteen lanes execute each matching shuffle with the same mask and width, including lanes without partners; the conditional addition does not skip a shuffle. The synchronized intrinsics provide the required rendezvous and register exchange without assuming implicit lockstep execution. In particular, reading oneself does not double-count anything because `has_partner` is false and the addition is skipped.

