```
When `partner >= 19u`, `has_partner` is false, so `source` equals `lane`. Under the original contract, that caller is physical lane 0–18, its bit is set in `mask = 0x0007ffffu`, and all nineteen named lanes execute this same shuffle with that mask; therefore the self-source participates.

The shuffle returns that lane’s current `sum`, but the false `has_partner` condition skips the addition entirely. Its `sum` remains unchanged, so reading itself does not double-count its input or any inputs already accumulated in its partial sum. For example, lane 18 at offset 16 computes partner 34, reads source 18, and performs no addition. It still executes every subsequent reduction shuffle and the original final broadcast from lane 0.
